WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.240 --> 00:00:04.073
- Goals.

00:00:04.073 --> 00:00:04.906
- Set your goals.

00:00:04.906 --> 00:00:05.739
- Setting goals.

00:00:05.739 --> 00:00:06.572
- Set goals.

00:00:06.572 --> 00:00:07.405
- Set little goals.

00:00:07.405 --> 00:00:08.238
- Goal setting.

00:00:08.238 --> 00:00:09.071
- Set some goals.

00:00:09.071 --> 00:00:09.904
- Set goals.

00:00:09.904 --> 00:00:10.737
- Goals.

00:00:10.737 --> 00:00:11.570
- Hello Believe Nation.

00:00:11.570 --> 00:00:12.403
My name is Evan Carmichael.

00:00:12.403 --> 00:00:14.889
My one word is believe and
I believe that entrepreneurs

00:00:14.889 --> 00:00:17.759
will solve all of the
worlds' major problems.

00:00:17.759 --> 00:00:19.954
So, to help you on your journey
today we're going to learn

00:00:19.954 --> 00:00:22.053
how you can set goals.

00:00:22.053 --> 00:00:24.228
If you're watching and you
hear something that really

00:00:24.228 --> 00:00:26.500
resonates with you, please
leave it down in the comments

00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:29.251
below, put quotes around it,
you might win a prize, but

00:00:29.251 --> 00:00:31.009
also, when you write it
down, it's much more likely

00:00:31.009 --> 00:00:33.568
to stay with yourself as well.

00:00:33.568 --> 00:00:34.947
Enjoy.

00:00:34.947 --> 00:00:37.780
(uplifting music)

00:00:46.016 --> 00:00:49.098
- I got an older white male,
he's probably in his 60's

00:00:49.098 --> 00:00:53.523
maybe, and my man says to me,
"I heard what you said ET,

00:00:53.523 --> 00:00:55.636
but how do you sustain it?"

00:00:55.636 --> 00:00:58.373
I'm like, "okay, all right
say it again because I want

00:00:58.373 --> 00:01:00.023
to make sure I'm hearing
what you're saying".

00:01:00.023 --> 00:01:02.388
He's like, "you talk about
going 120, you talk about going

00:01:02.388 --> 00:01:04.996
hard, you talk about having
what you want, being what you

00:01:04.996 --> 00:01:07.476
want, do what you want, okay
I get it, but how do you

00:01:07.476 --> 00:01:08.605
sustain it?"

00:01:08.605 --> 00:01:10.441
I'm thinking is that a real question?

00:01:10.441 --> 00:01:12.537
I said, "listen to me very
closely, how did I start

00:01:12.537 --> 00:01:14.140
this whole presentation off?"

00:01:14.140 --> 00:01:16.469
He said, "write down the
people's name that you love."

00:01:16.469 --> 00:01:18.880
I said, "duh, if you're waking
up every day and thinking

00:01:18.880 --> 00:01:21.722
about your wife, duh, how
do you not sustain it?"

00:01:21.722 --> 00:01:24.164
If you wake up every day and
you're looking at your son,

00:01:24.164 --> 00:01:25.459
how do you not sustain it?

00:01:25.459 --> 00:01:27.954
You think I'm going to put
my kid's life in the hands

00:01:27.954 --> 00:01:29.771
of some other man?

00:01:29.771 --> 00:01:32.365
You think that's my role as a father?

00:01:32.365 --> 00:01:35.772
You think my role is to
allow my kids to come here,

00:01:35.772 --> 00:01:38.039
and pay all this money to go
to school, and do everything

00:01:38.039 --> 00:01:39.290
they did and now they've got

00:01:39.290 --> 00:01:41.222
to go beg somebody else for a job?

00:01:41.222 --> 00:01:43.766
That's not my role or responsibility.

00:01:43.766 --> 00:01:44.848
Sustain it?

00:01:44.848 --> 00:01:45.681
What do you mean?

00:01:45.681 --> 00:01:46.952
How do you not sustain it?

00:01:46.952 --> 00:01:49.734
I asked you, "why are you not pumped up?"

00:01:49.734 --> 00:01:51.206
Why you have days off?

00:01:51.206 --> 00:01:53.403
I'm asking you why you give 70%.

00:01:53.403 --> 00:01:55.236
You don't love nobody?

00:01:56.431 --> 00:01:57.939
Is there not somebody
that you don't love more

00:01:57.939 --> 00:01:59.444
than yourself?

00:01:59.444 --> 00:02:01.748
Is there not somebody
that you're waking up for?

00:02:01.748 --> 00:02:03.991
Is there not somebody you're grinding for?

00:02:03.991 --> 00:02:05.902
Somebody told me that
they get distracted easy.

00:02:05.902 --> 00:02:07.080
Let me tell you something,
the reason why you're

00:02:07.080 --> 00:02:08.441
getting distracted easy is
because you don't got eight

00:02:08.441 --> 00:02:10.533
or nine things you wake
up to every single day

00:02:10.533 --> 00:02:11.664
and say, "I've got to go get that".

00:02:11.664 --> 00:02:13.364
Many of you are getting
distracted because you don't

00:02:13.364 --> 00:02:17.658
have something that's
stronger than the distraction.

00:02:17.658 --> 00:02:20.189
You need something stronger
than the distraction.

00:02:20.189 --> 00:02:21.900
You're getting distracted with parties.

00:02:21.900 --> 00:02:23.476
You're getting distracted with smoking.

00:02:23.476 --> 00:02:25.004
You're getting distracted with drinking.

00:02:25.004 --> 00:02:26.586
You're getting distracted with sleeping.

00:02:26.586 --> 00:02:28.130
You're getting distracted
with video games.

00:02:28.130 --> 00:02:28.963
Why?

00:02:28.963 --> 00:02:31.839
Because the video game is
stronger than your goal.

00:02:31.839 --> 00:02:33.079
I tell my homies all the
time, bro, if it don't have

00:02:33.079 --> 00:02:34.497
anything to do with, you all be playing.

00:02:34.497 --> 00:02:37.244
I'm like, if it ain't about the money.

00:02:37.244 --> 00:02:38.312
You're just singing it.

00:02:38.312 --> 00:02:40.522
I'm for real; don't be blowing me up.

00:02:40.522 --> 00:02:42.652
- It's easy to pull things back.

00:02:42.652 --> 00:02:44.881
It's very hard to ramp things up.

00:02:44.881 --> 00:02:46.984
I'd rather start with
something that's too big, and

00:02:46.984 --> 00:02:49.060
pull it back into reality
than start with something

00:02:49.060 --> 00:02:52.977
that's so easy that you
can't really get it up.

00:02:53.914 --> 00:02:57.403
For example, don't set
your goals realistically,

00:02:57.403 --> 00:02:59.680
set them entirely unrealistically.

00:02:59.680 --> 00:03:02.730
Shoot for 80 and be
disappointed when you hit 70,

00:03:02.730 --> 00:03:04.920
as opposed to shooting
for 20 and being ecstatic

00:03:04.920 --> 00:03:05.795
when you hit 21.

00:03:05.795 --> 00:03:06.920
We beat our goal!

00:03:06.920 --> 00:03:10.273
Yeah, but it was a very low goal.

00:03:10.273 --> 00:03:14.440
I think to be frustrated in
achieving something rather than

00:03:15.513 --> 00:03:20.222
ecstatic and achieving less
is a better way to live.

00:03:20.222 --> 00:03:23.695
Not to mention, you achieve more.

00:03:23.695 --> 00:03:27.431
So, I'm a great believer
in the greater good.

00:03:27.431 --> 00:03:31.929
Those things are so
big; they're ridiculous.

00:03:31.929 --> 00:03:36.423
My goal, is a hundred-year
goal, is called world peace.

00:03:36.423 --> 00:03:39.590
(laughs) So daunting,

00:03:40.902 --> 00:03:41.829
but that's the idea.

00:03:41.829 --> 00:03:44.976
If I fail, and I certainly
want to achieve it in my

00:03:44.976 --> 00:03:48.346
lifetime, I'd like to think
that what I'll contribute

00:03:48.346 --> 00:03:52.355
towards that ridiculous,
idealistic, nonsense goal

00:03:52.355 --> 00:03:54.578
will be more than if I say,
"if I can just be happy

00:03:54.578 --> 00:03:57.161
by myself, in my little house".

00:03:58.047 --> 00:04:00.891
That's nice and all, but I
like the idea of contributing

00:04:00.891 --> 00:04:02.494
to your neighbor as well.

00:04:02.494 --> 00:04:03.727
- I don't want to be called an actor.

00:04:03.727 --> 00:04:05.177
I don't want to be called a star.

00:04:05.177 --> 00:04:06.904
I don't want to have a label.

00:04:06.904 --> 00:04:09.523
I want to have a legacy.

00:04:09.523 --> 00:04:12.606
I want to be known as someone who has

00:04:14.135 --> 00:04:15.662
goals and achieves them.

00:04:15.662 --> 00:04:18.592
Whatever they might be,
wherever they might be,

00:04:18.592 --> 00:04:20.122
I want to be limitless.

00:04:20.122 --> 00:04:22.698
I want to break stereotypes.

00:04:22.698 --> 00:04:26.357
I want to go where no man
or woman has gone before.

00:04:26.357 --> 00:04:29.492
It might be a scary path, it
might be a path that no one's

00:04:29.492 --> 00:04:32.742
taken, but at least it'll be just mine.

00:04:35.897 --> 00:04:39.541
I had the worst self-esteem
when I was a kid.

00:04:39.541 --> 00:04:42.508
I was made fun of because
of the way I talked,

00:04:42.508 --> 00:04:44.010
because of where I came from.

00:04:44.010 --> 00:04:47.210
I was made fun of on every
level, and the only way you

00:04:47.210 --> 00:04:51.075
can change that is setting
goals for yourself and saying

00:04:51.075 --> 00:04:54.115
I will be the best version of me.

00:04:54.115 --> 00:04:56.971
When I was 18, I started
doing movies, I gave myself

00:04:56.971 --> 00:05:00.585
a year and a half, and I
said, "if I sense that I'm not

00:05:00.585 --> 00:05:04.087
good at what I'm doing, and
I don't see something opening

00:05:04.087 --> 00:05:06.916
up for me, I'm going
to go back to college".

00:05:06.916 --> 00:05:07.981
I always had a plan B.

00:05:07.981 --> 00:05:09.713
I still always have a plan B.

00:05:09.713 --> 00:05:11.515
That's what I always tell young people.

00:05:11.515 --> 00:05:15.527
Life doesn't end, it just keeps moving.

00:05:15.527 --> 00:05:18.086
You have to put your blinkers
on and find what you do best,

00:05:18.086 --> 00:05:19.846
and just keep moving.

00:05:19.846 --> 00:05:22.291
- I want you to start
seeing something bigger.

00:05:22.291 --> 00:05:23.610
I know you're all successful.

00:05:23.610 --> 00:05:27.198
I'm talking about something
really big for your life.

00:05:27.198 --> 00:05:31.365
In order to do that, you
have to answer this question,

00:05:32.409 --> 00:05:35.213
what do you really want?

00:05:35.213 --> 00:05:37.720
Now, I'm not talking
about something small.

00:05:37.720 --> 00:05:40.332
I'm not talking about a little haiku.

00:05:40.332 --> 00:05:42.792
I'm not talking about
renovating your kitchen.

00:05:42.792 --> 00:05:44.154
I'm not talking about signing

00:05:44.154 --> 00:05:46.819
on ten new customers this month.

00:05:46.819 --> 00:05:50.069
I'm talking about what you really want.

00:05:51.929 --> 00:05:56.705
Three years ago, I was a
lawyer and a business coach,

00:05:56.705 --> 00:05:59.023
working with private
clients and big corporations

00:05:59.023 --> 00:06:00.747
all over the country.

00:06:00.747 --> 00:06:04.706
I came to a seminar, just like
this one, a big leadership

00:06:04.706 --> 00:06:06.946
seminar and I went there with my husband.

00:06:06.946 --> 00:06:08.663
We're both business
owners, and I went because

00:06:08.663 --> 00:06:11.182
I wanted to be more successful.

00:06:11.182 --> 00:06:14.345
I went because I wanted
to make even more money

00:06:14.345 --> 00:06:15.178
than I already did.

00:06:15.178 --> 00:06:17.679
I was sitting exactly where
you are, in fact, I was

00:06:17.679 --> 00:06:21.013
sitting about 15 rows back,
right where that woman with

00:06:21.013 --> 00:06:25.203
her hand, yeah you, she's
like, "hi", was sitting.

00:06:25.203 --> 00:06:27.130
I was taking notes, and
I'm like, okay, I'm here

00:06:27.130 --> 00:06:29.164
to make more money.

00:06:29.164 --> 00:06:32.694
Then all of the sudden,
she walked on stage.

00:06:32.694 --> 00:06:34.361
That is Martha Beck.

00:06:36.122 --> 00:06:38.944
She writes a column for Oprah Winfrey.

00:06:38.944 --> 00:06:41.611
She travels around the country speaking.

00:06:41.611 --> 00:06:43.989
She's a best-selling author.

00:06:43.989 --> 00:06:48.156
When she walked on stage, I
literally stopped listening.

00:06:49.465 --> 00:06:53.407
Please keep listening
to me right now, okay.

00:06:53.407 --> 00:06:54.240
It hit me.

00:06:55.495 --> 00:06:59.042
I said, "I want to be doing that".

00:06:59.042 --> 00:07:00.396
I'm ready for a bigger stage.

00:07:00.396 --> 00:07:01.229
That's it.

00:07:02.653 --> 00:07:05.630
What's so interesting about
when you answer that question,

00:07:05.630 --> 00:07:10.538
is that you don't answer it
up here, you answer it here.

00:07:10.538 --> 00:07:12.857
That's how you see something
bigger for yourself.

00:07:12.857 --> 00:07:14.921
You guys are really cute
because everybody is like,

00:07:14.921 --> 00:07:17.878
I don't see it, I don't see
anything for myself right now.

00:07:17.878 --> 00:07:19.392
I'm just confused.

00:07:19.392 --> 00:07:21.596
I thought I knew what I wanted.

00:07:21.596 --> 00:07:24.013
Now Mel, I'm not really sure.

00:07:25.835 --> 00:07:29.264
Right now, the economy is so bad.

00:07:29.264 --> 00:07:32.634
It's so bad that even if
you're successful, I know

00:07:32.634 --> 00:07:35.665
sometimes I feel embarrassed
talking about my success

00:07:35.665 --> 00:07:37.301
around some of my friends because I know

00:07:37.301 --> 00:07:39.742
that they're really struggling.

00:07:39.742 --> 00:07:44.585
I get calls every day into
the radio show, people saying

00:07:44.585 --> 00:07:46.846
I've got this great idea,
but I just don't know

00:07:46.846 --> 00:07:49.412
if it's the right time.

00:07:49.412 --> 00:07:50.367
You know what I say to them?

00:07:50.367 --> 00:07:52.879
I say, yeah, you know, you're right.

00:07:52.879 --> 00:07:54.304
The recession, it's huge.

00:07:54.304 --> 00:07:55.468
You should wait.

00:07:55.468 --> 00:07:58.877
Those dreams, yeah, put them on hold.

00:07:58.877 --> 00:08:00.635
You should stay in that
job you can't stand

00:08:00.635 --> 00:08:01.811
just a little bit longer.

00:08:01.811 --> 00:08:04.731
You've got college bills to pay.

00:08:04.731 --> 00:08:05.911
What you're doing, it's fine.

00:08:05.911 --> 00:08:07.907
You're busy, right?

00:08:07.907 --> 00:08:10.593
That guy you're dating,
he's good enough for you.

00:08:10.593 --> 00:08:14.093
But, for the people in this room, bologna.

00:08:15.477 --> 00:08:19.421
That's right, you know
exactly what you want,

00:08:19.421 --> 00:08:23.588
and the only thing that you
need to do is to admit it.

00:08:24.659 --> 00:08:26.609
This may sound weird because
I know most of you came

00:08:26.609 --> 00:08:28.206
in here because you're like,
"I know what I want, I'm

00:08:28.206 --> 00:08:30.540
here at Success to try to figure it out.

00:08:30.540 --> 00:08:34.221
I'm talking about something bigger,

00:08:34.221 --> 00:08:35.221
much bigger.

00:08:37.693 --> 00:08:41.573
I'll admit to you what
it is that I'm up to.

00:08:41.573 --> 00:08:46.089
The truth is, it's embarrassing
because when you lock

00:08:46.089 --> 00:08:48.442
onto something way bigger
than where you're at,

00:08:48.442 --> 00:08:52.633
it is down right embarrassing
to tell people because

00:08:52.633 --> 00:08:54.654
you're not there yet.

00:08:54.654 --> 00:08:57.473
At this rate, I've already
admitted to you that I stalked

00:08:57.473 --> 00:09:00.085
Martha Beck, and that I
brought a haiku to the best

00:09:00.085 --> 00:09:02.062
lit agent in the country,
so I've got nothing to lose

00:09:02.062 --> 00:09:03.229
at this point.

00:09:04.152 --> 00:09:05.819
This is what I want.

00:09:10.729 --> 00:09:13.043
Well, not him, I'm married.

00:09:13.043 --> 00:09:15.613
I want what he's got.

00:09:15.613 --> 00:09:17.780
I want 600 radio stations.

00:09:18.822 --> 00:09:21.922
I want two million listeners,
and I could certainly

00:09:21.922 --> 00:09:24.239
deal with the $400 million salary.

00:09:24.239 --> 00:09:28.391
In fact, if I got it, I'd
renovate everybody's kitchen.

00:09:28.391 --> 00:09:31.992
The thing is though, that's
so interesting about this,

00:09:31.992 --> 00:09:34.644
is that I didn't pick him.

00:09:34.644 --> 00:09:38.961
I'm not looking to become a
cigar-smoking conservative

00:09:38.961 --> 00:09:41.653
political guy that stirs the pot

00:09:41.653 --> 00:09:43.799
and makes everybody all mad.

00:09:43.799 --> 00:09:45.764
I'm the liberal lifestyle
gal that's trying

00:09:45.764 --> 00:09:49.524
to help people out, but
what I want to do is I want

00:09:49.524 --> 00:09:52.632
to use radio to entertain people and

00:09:52.632 --> 00:09:55.215
help them achieve their dreams.

00:09:56.536 --> 00:09:59.556
When I really think about
it, he's the one that's

00:09:59.556 --> 00:10:00.639
in the front.

00:10:01.660 --> 00:10:03.506
I want to not only reach what he is doing,

00:10:03.506 --> 00:10:05.342
I want to surpass him.

00:10:05.342 --> 00:10:07.568
Do you think I like it
when my friends come over

00:10:07.568 --> 00:10:10.797
to my office in Boston at
my house, and they're like,

00:10:10.797 --> 00:10:14.130
"what is that guy doing on your board?'.

00:10:15.304 --> 00:10:17.137
No, it's embarrassing.

00:10:18.257 --> 00:10:21.086
When you admit the big
thing that you're up to,

00:10:21.086 --> 00:10:22.616
it's embarrassing.

00:10:22.616 --> 00:10:25.929
I have 40 stations, he's got 600.

00:10:25.929 --> 00:10:27.429
There's a big gap.

00:10:28.618 --> 00:10:32.570
So, admitting where you want
to get to is embarrassing,

00:10:32.570 --> 00:10:34.089
but you've got to do it.

00:10:34.089 --> 00:10:37.591
- You see, the beautiful part
about goals, and understanding

00:10:37.591 --> 00:10:39.983
it is goals are not to get.

00:10:39.983 --> 00:10:43.473
You don't get set goals for acquisition.

00:10:43.473 --> 00:10:46.130
You set goals to grow.

00:10:46.130 --> 00:10:49.737
You set goals to reach
inside, stretch, and go where

00:10:49.737 --> 00:10:51.818
you've never been.

00:10:51.818 --> 00:10:54.366
You set goals to take you
to a place you've never gone

00:10:54.366 --> 00:10:57.283
before, and you grow as a human being.

00:10:57.283 --> 00:10:59.597
You don't accept it, you never go back.

00:10:59.597 --> 00:11:02.347
- Now, I don't watch TV too much.

00:11:03.429 --> 00:11:05.271
It's hard because most of the
time I watch a lot of ESPN,

00:11:05.271 --> 00:11:06.604
but not anymore.

00:11:07.888 --> 00:11:11.023
To be honest with you, try
to stay focused and set

00:11:11.023 --> 00:11:13.917
little goals for myself every day.

00:11:13.917 --> 00:11:15.563
Get a little bit better.

00:11:15.563 --> 00:11:18.136
Learn one new thing and
improve in one way every day

00:11:18.136 --> 00:11:19.546
when I step out here.

00:11:19.546 --> 00:11:21.143
When you set all those
little goals and you keep

00:11:21.143 --> 00:11:23.128
hitting them, then you're
constantly going to keep getting

00:11:23.128 --> 00:11:26.729
better and not worry
about everything else.

00:11:26.729 --> 00:11:28.393
just let that take care of itself.

00:11:28.393 --> 00:11:30.190
Worry about what I can control.

00:11:30.190 --> 00:11:32.690
First, let me say that I think

00:11:34.328 --> 00:11:38.495
the goals, pretty much set
the tone for everything else.

00:11:48.234 --> 00:11:52.006
I guess when you think about goal setting,

00:11:52.006 --> 00:11:55.756
and when you really
allow your goals to start

00:11:57.381 --> 00:12:01.251
becoming the lead to manage your steps

00:12:01.251 --> 00:12:04.251
then your life path starts to become

00:12:06.601 --> 00:12:10.351
guided, and not just
haphazard and by chance.

00:12:17.425 --> 00:12:21.008
Your goals become the
predetermined address

00:12:25.606 --> 00:12:29.689
that would serve as a
destination, an end result.

00:12:30.891 --> 00:12:35.058
Now, with at least that,
you're able to make decisions

00:12:37.407 --> 00:12:41.407
and map out a course,
step-by-step, if you will,

00:12:42.952 --> 00:12:45.134
that will help get you there.

00:12:45.134 --> 00:12:48.956
The really cool thing about
goal setting is that even

00:12:48.956 --> 00:12:53.123
if you do not have all the
information beyond the address,

00:12:54.961 --> 00:12:58.544
like, what streets,
where and when to turn,

00:13:00.412 --> 00:13:05.275
with having the address, you
can always type in the GPS

00:13:05.275 --> 00:13:07.442
coordinate and pretty much

00:13:09.636 --> 00:13:11.976
take advantage of other

00:13:11.976 --> 00:13:13.793
sensibilities that can help point you

00:13:13.793 --> 00:13:15.710
in the right direction.

00:13:16.585 --> 00:13:19.306
A lot of times, you don't
really need to have all

00:13:19.306 --> 00:13:23.767
of the guess work predetermined
and already figured out.

00:13:23.767 --> 00:13:28.648
Once you have the address,
you're that much closer

00:13:28.648 --> 00:13:32.189
to being able to get
where you're trying to go.

00:13:32.189 --> 00:13:35.928
As an athlete on stage,
that's kind of what I'm using

00:13:35.928 --> 00:13:39.261
to help get me where I feel I need to be

00:13:42.075 --> 00:13:44.825
to perform at maximum efficiency.

00:13:49.439 --> 00:13:52.522
Goal setting is very, very important.

00:13:54.057 --> 00:13:58.135
It's been very, very
critical in helping me get

00:13:58.135 --> 00:14:02.302
from the beginning of my
career to where I am presently.

00:14:03.577 --> 00:14:05.402
- You had a plan; the
remarkable thing to me was

00:14:05.402 --> 00:14:08.226
at 22, 23 years old, that your plan

00:14:08.226 --> 00:14:10.153
was completely laid out.

00:14:10.153 --> 00:14:12.087
In reading your book, you
knew, I was going to take

00:14:12.087 --> 00:14:12.990
this amount of money.

00:14:12.990 --> 00:14:14.980
Your plan was to make
three El Mariachi movies.

00:14:14.980 --> 00:14:16.723
- Yeah, the thing is, if
you want to get somewhere,

00:14:16.723 --> 00:14:18.604
you've really got to set
some goals for yourself.

00:14:18.604 --> 00:14:20.420
They won't ever happen
the way you planned, but

00:14:20.420 --> 00:14:21.253
at least you ...

00:14:21.253 --> 00:14:22.433
- Don't I know that.

00:14:22.433 --> 00:14:25.086
- You'll step forward
in a positive direction

00:14:25.086 --> 00:14:27.714
that may take you some
place better by accident.

00:14:27.714 --> 00:14:31.881
- You just have to ... it's
not easy to see beyond where

00:14:32.923 --> 00:14:36.599
you are, but you have to try
to see beyond where you are.

00:14:36.599 --> 00:14:38.375
Try to set goals beyond where you are.

00:14:38.375 --> 00:14:41.113
Think about ways that you can break out

00:14:41.113 --> 00:14:42.173
and make a difference.

00:14:42.173 --> 00:14:43.280
That's what I did.

00:14:43.280 --> 00:14:46.232
I had some great people around
me, my family, teachers,

00:14:46.232 --> 00:14:50.057
people that believed in
me and encouraged me.

00:14:50.057 --> 00:14:52.317
Sent me off to an Ivy League school, and

00:14:52.317 --> 00:14:53.650
I figured it out after that.

00:14:53.650 --> 00:14:56.307
- But, why, some say, the moon?

00:14:56.307 --> 00:14:59.332
Why choose this as our goal?

00:14:59.332 --> 00:15:03.751
They may well ask, why
climb the highest mountain?

00:15:03.751 --> 00:15:06.668
Why 35 years ago, fly the Atlantic?

00:15:07.677 --> 00:15:09.909
Why does Rice play Texas?

00:15:09.909 --> 00:15:12.690
We choose to go to the moon.

00:15:12.690 --> 00:15:15.023
We choose to go to the moon.

00:15:20.669 --> 00:15:23.813
We choose to go to the moon
in this decade and do the

00:15:23.813 --> 00:15:27.609
other things, not because they
are easy, but because they

00:15:27.609 --> 00:15:31.776
are hard, because that goal
will serve to organize and

00:15:32.791 --> 00:15:37.044
measure the best of our energies
and skills, because that

00:15:37.044 --> 00:15:40.546
challenge is one that
we're willing to accept.

00:15:40.546 --> 00:15:45.211
One we are unwilling to postpone,
and one we intend to win,

00:15:45.211 --> 00:15:47.040
and the others too.

00:15:47.040 --> 00:15:48.321
- Thank you guys so much for watching.

00:15:48.321 --> 00:15:49.461
I hope you enjoyed it.

00:15:49.461 --> 00:15:51.494
I'd love to know, what did
you take from this video

00:15:51.494 --> 00:15:54.337
that you're going to immediately
apply somehow to your

00:15:54.337 --> 00:15:55.961
life or to your business?

00:15:55.961 --> 00:15:57.390
Leave it down in the comments below.

00:15:57.390 --> 00:15:59.585
I'm really want to see
what you have to say.

00:15:59.585 --> 00:16:01.403
I also want to give a
quick shout to Luis Lopez

00:16:01.403 --> 00:16:03.685
from The Better Men Project.

00:16:03.685 --> 00:16:06.019
Luis, thank you so much for
picking up a copy of my book,

00:16:06.019 --> 00:16:07.297
Your One Word.

00:16:07.297 --> 00:16:09.377
I really appreciate the
support and I'm glad you

00:16:09.377 --> 00:16:10.954
enjoyed your book.

00:16:10.954 --> 00:16:13.906
- [Announcer] If you could
describe yourself with one word,

00:16:13.906 --> 00:16:14.949
what would it be?

00:16:14.949 --> 00:16:16.393
- So thank you guys for watching,

00:16:16.393 --> 00:16:17.537
I believe in you.

00:16:17.537 --> 00:16:19.808
I hope you continue to believe
in yourself and whatever

00:16:19.808 --> 00:16:21.869
your one word is.

00:16:21.869 --> 00:16:24.286
Much love, I'll see you soon.

